<title>UK: EX-DIVIDENDS TO TAKE 15.41 POINTS OFF FTSE, AUG 11. [CORRECTED 14:07 GMT]</title>
<headline>EX-DIVIDENDS TO TAKE 15.41 POINTS OFF FTSE, AUG 11. [CORRECTED 14:07 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following FTSE 100 stocks will go ex-dividend on August 11 and analysts estimate the effect will be to take 15.41 points off the index on Monday.</p>
<p>(correcting number of FTSE points from 28.88 to 15.41 in headline and</p>
<p>first paragraph )</p>
<p>					    DIVIDEND   INDEX</p>
<p>					     (PENCE)    EFFECT</p>
<p>COMPANY					Net	 Net</p>
<p>* Abbey National			  10.20	0.816</p>
<p>* B.A.T. Industries		    10.00	1.770</p>
<p>* British Petroleum Co.		   5.50	1.782</p>
<p>* British Telecommunications     (a) 11.95     17.818</p>
<p>(correcting BT dividend effect to 11.95p from 48.95p)</p>
<p>* Glaxo Wellcome		   (b) 15.00	3.045</p>
<p>* Lloyds TSB Group			5.30	1.627</p>
<p>* National Westminster Bank	   10.60	1.028</p>
<p>* Siebe				(b)  9.80	0.284</p>
<p>* TI Group			     (b)  5.10	0.138</p>
<p>* Tomkins				   8.39	0.571</p>
<p>(a) Dividend amount for British Telecommunications includes a special</p>
<p>dividend of 35p.</p>
<p>(b) Dividend amounts for Glaxo Wellcome, Siebe and TI Group are Foreign</p>
<p>Income Dividends (FIDs) only.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7954</p>
</text>
